### One payload carrying NINE distinct problems. The claim is that the refusal names every one of
### them — not the first, and not a representative sample. §0 principle 4's reader is an agent, and a
### 422 reporting one problem per round trip costs it one request per mistake.
###
### The problems, one per field so nothing is double-counted:
###   reference     - does not match the declared `work-order-ref` format
###   title         - longer than the declared maxLength of 120
###   status        - not one of the declared enum values
###   priority      - required, and absent
###   quoted_price  - three fractional digits where the field declares a scale of 2
###   contact_email - not an email
###   external_ref  - readOnly, so a caller may read it and never write it
###   customer_id   - a ref to a row that does not exist
###   region_id     - the same, on the second ref, so "every violation" covers a repeated kind
# @name ManyViolations
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "NOT-A-REFERENCE",
  "title": "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
  "status": "pending",
  "quoted_price": 1.234,
  "contact_email": "not-an-email",
  "external_ref": "mine-to-set",
  "access_code": "PROBE",
  "customer_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000c1",
  "region_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000e1"
}

### A key the entity does not declare is refused with 422 rather than ignored
# @name UnknownField
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-3001",
  "title": "Unknown field",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 3,
  "access_code": "PROBE",
  "customer_id": "{{CustomerAcmeId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}",
  "urgency": "very"
}

### The refusal kinds are different slugs, because their fixes are different: a body the schema
### refuses is `validation`, a query string the parser refuses is `malformed-query`.
# @name MalformedQueryKind
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=notanumber
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### After nine violations and an unknown key, no row was written
# @name NothingWasWritten
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=100&order=reference.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
